<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 14:22:52 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Cyprus: Ferry capsizes with hundreds on board</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-cyprus-ferry-capsizes-with-hundreds-of-board</link><description>
Authorities say at least six people have died after a catamaran-style ferry carrying 267 passengers and crew capsized off the coast of northern Cyprus. The Turkish ambassador to Nicosia said 172 people had been rescued, with some taken to hospital, while 89 remain missing. The death toll has since risen to seven, according to the latest figures. France 24 correspondent Jasper Mortimer reports the latest from Ankara, Turkey.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6bf8b1f6-a474-11f1-865f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/cyprus-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6bf8b1f6-a474-11f1-865f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/cyprus-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0fa85122-a474-11f1-8c2b-21aa33126e34</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:13:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Hopes fade for thousands still missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-hopes-fade-for-thousands-still-missing</link><description>
Four days have passed since catastrophic floods killed more than 750 people. More than 3,000 people are still missing, and hopes of finding survivors are fading. The situation remains concerning, with more heavy rain and flooding expected across the region. France 24 correspondent Shahzaib Wahlah brings us the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b34fa4c-a46f-11f1-877a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-140709-140945-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b34fa4c-a46f-11f1-877a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-140709-140945-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a069a03a-a46f-11f1-92e1-d3a0eb937380</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:11:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Norway’s New King breaks silence after father’s death</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-norway-s-new-king-breaks-silence-after-father-s-death</link><description>
Norway’s new king addressed the nation for the first time since taking the throne, paying tribute to his 89-year-old father, who died the previous day. Morgan Ayre has the details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a993afb4-a467-11f1-9ea0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-131803-131951-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a993afb4-a467-11f1-9ea0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-131803-131951-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aeacd174-a467-11f1-86d5-6f9a81a1cdb5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:31:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pacific Summit opens amid Taiwan row</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pacific-summit-opens-amid-taiwan-row</link><description>
The annual Pacific Islands Forum begins on Monday in Palau, bringing together the 18-member intergovernmental organisation to discuss regional cooperation and security. On Sunday, Taiwan’s Foreign Minister Lin Chia-lung joined Palau President Surangel Whipps at a ceremony to hand over a fleet of electric buses donated by Taipei. China has criticised Taiwan’s participation in the event. Charles Parton, Senior Associate Fellow at the Royal United Services Institute (RUSI), shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e6171ae-a467-11f1-8f41-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-130734-131128-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e6171ae-a467-11f1-8f41-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-130734-131128-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43a253ae-a467-11f1-b923-f91f97a00f18</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:29:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ferry carrying more than 260 people capsizes off northern Cyprus</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ferry-carrying-more-than-260-people-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus</link><description>
Authorities say several people have died after a ferry accident off the coast of northern Cyprus. The catamaran-style vessel was carrying nearly 270 passengers and crew when it capsized. Turkey’s ambassador to Nicosia said many of those on board were rescued, while some were taken to hospital. France 24 correspondent Nathalie Savaricas reports the latest. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edbb990e-a46c-11f1-98b8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-140136-140448-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edbb990e-a46c-11f1-98b8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-140136-140448-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2429270-a46c-11f1-9bfb-d3a0eb937380</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:27:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Rescue under way after ferry with more than 260 on board capsizes off northern Cyprus</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus</link><description>
At least seven people died when a ferry carrying more than 260 people capsized off the coast of northern Cyprus on Sunday, according to local authorities. Rescue crews were dispatched to the scene, with footage showing passengers in life jackets in the water around the overturned vessel. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83fcbb98-a475-11f1-a4bf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242466294401.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83fcbb98-a475-11f1-a4bf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242466294401.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b37d1b2-a469-11f1-b2de-6f9a81a1cdb5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:08:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83fcbb98-a475-11f1-a4bf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242466294401.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US and Venezuela seal 25-year oil deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-venezuela-seal-25-year-oil-deal</link><description>
US President Donald Trump has called it “the biggest oil deal in world history”, while Venezuela’s interim president has assured the public that the country will retain control of its oil under the agreement. The “historic” 25-year deal with Washington involves 65 billion barrels of Venezuelan oil and aims to allow the country to develop its oil industry while preserving “ownership of and sovereignty” over its resources, Rodriguez said in a televised address. Rachael Griffiths has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4491d1dc-a466-11f1-9433-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-121001-121146-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4491d1dc-a466-11f1-9433-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-121001-121146-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49e481ac-a466-11f1-9dcb-6f9a81a1cdb5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:34:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Argentines march on Peter Thiel's mansion</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-march-on-peter-thiel-s-mansion</link><description>
In Argentina, protesters marched toward a mansion reportedly purchased by American tech billionaire Peter Thiel. Activists accuse Thiel of seeking to profit from the country’s natural resources and wielding excessive political influence in the South American nation. Peter O'Brien reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af588c0a-a456-11f1-957d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110822-111000-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af588c0a-a456-11f1-957d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110822-111000-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b479fef8-a456-11f1-945c-57cf20512793</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:06:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Thousands still missing as death toll rises</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-death-toll-rises</link><description>
Nepalese authorities announced on Sunday that the provisional death toll from the devastating floods had risen to more than 730, with nearly 2,500 people still missing.

Among the thousands of people missing is the husband of a 22-year-old woman, who is still waiting for him to return. Like tens of thousands of Nepalese people in recent days, she went to one of the country’s medical centres to find out whether her husband was among those whose bodies had been recovered in recent days. Caitlin Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac96234e-a454-11f1-b965-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110309-110452-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac96234e-a454-11f1-b965-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110309-110452-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2739594-a454-11f1-baaa-49bcf89cf529</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:04:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Iceland rejects restarting EU accession talks in referendum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">9b2ad996-a455-11f1-9651-57cf20512793</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:31:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Iceland rejects restarting EU accession talks in referendum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum</link><description>
Icelanders voted to reject reopening EU membership talks, official results showed Sunday, dealing a blow to the government's push to join the bloc and handing a win to those who argued the country's prized fishing waters were too important to risk. The results will disappoint Brussels, which had hoped to welcome the Nordic country as a new member.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4688a00c-a447-11f1-90f2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T185525Z-1431504769-RC2H8NA5PMLX-RTRMADP-3-ICELAND-EU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4688a00c-a447-11f1-90f2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T185525Z-1431504769-RC2H8NA5PMLX-RTRMADP-3-ICELAND-EU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ebb89a6-a447-11f1-a901-75564c8cf08f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:30:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4688a00c-a447-11f1-90f2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T185525Z-1431504769-RC2H8NA5PMLX-RTRMADP-3-ICELAND-EU.jpg">© Leonhard Foeger, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Harry Potter: Versailles turns into wizarding school for a day</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260830-harry-potter-versailles-turns-into-wizarding-school-for-a-day</link><description>
Accio nostalgia! ⚡️
 
Can you believe it’s been 25 years since Harry Potter first hit the big screen? To celebrate, French fans turned the Palace of Versailles into Hogwarts for a unique reunion.
 
📹 France 24 was there to capture the magic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5a94b0a-a455-11f1-bd7e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-HP.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5a94b0a-a455-11f1-bd7e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-HP.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b018f96a-a454-11f1-9d8f-49bcf89cf529</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:25:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Glacial collapse leaves 3,000 missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-glacial-collapse-leaves-3-000-missing</link><description>
Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4cbf6d4-a452-11f1-9422-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-100419-100544-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4cbf6d4-a452-11f1-9422-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-100419-100544-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">caebbc84-a452-11f1-b9bf-49bcf89cf529</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:16:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gunman kills one at Swiss rave party</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gunman-kills-one-at-swiss-rave-party</link><description>
A large-scale police operation is underway in Switzerland after a shooting at a rave in the town of Aarau, 46 kilometres west of Zurich, left one person dead and five others injured. Swiss daily Blick reported that some attendees initially mistook the gunshots for fireworks, until someone shouted, “everyone down”. Police are appealing to potential witnesses who may have photos or videos of the incident to come forward and share them with investigators. France 24 correspondent John Zarocostas reports from Zurich.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1241e324-a453-11f1-b1fe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/switzerland.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1241e324-a453-11f1-b1fe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/switzerland.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62b0252a-a451-11f1-b464-57cf20512793</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:14:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Vuelta: Pogacar’s terrifying crash, serious injuries and abandonment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260830-vuelta-pogacar-s-terrifying-crash-serious-injuries-and-abandonment</link><description>
Tadej Pogacar, who was comfortably leading the overall standings at the Vuelta a España, was forced to abandon on Saturday after a heavy crash during Stage 8. The Slovenian suffered multiple fractures and could even see his season come to an early end, with the World Championships looming at the end of September.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92f25eaa-a411-11f1-9a06-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2-9211811-1-big.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92f25eaa-a411-11f1-9a06-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2-9211811-1-big.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4396edd4-a412-11f1-b3e7-5f38413875fa</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:03:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French Presidential campaign heats up</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-presidential-campaign-heats-up</link><description>
There are just eight months to go before France’s presidential election, with the first round scheduled for April 18. The campaign is slowly heating up, with several political gatherings taking place this weekend. The Socialist Party wrapped up a two-day gathering on Saturday with a speech from party leader Olivier Faure, who has yet to officially announce his candidacy. Meanwhile, far-right figure Jordan Bardella made a campaign stop at a fair in the Champagne region. This comes after a first debate earlier this week between seven of the leading candidates, organised by business leaders. For an analysis of the current state of the race, we’re joined by Renaud Foucart, a Senior Lecturer in Economics at Lancaster University and one of our go-to analysts on French politics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bf85d84-a450-11f1-8d69-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/france-debat.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bf85d84-a450-11f1-8d69-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/france-debat.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e72e673a-a44c-11f1-9d4e-75564c8cf08f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:55:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Fridges for humans during heatwaves in Japan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/fridges-for-humans-during-heatwaves-in-japan</link><description>
A Japanese company has created a human-sized fridge, and workplaces across the country have been testing it out amid Japan’s current heatwave. Caitlin Brown has the story.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97560de8-a44d-11f1-a9d6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-092435-092603-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97560de8-a44d-11f1-a9d6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-092435-092603-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c299b28-a44d-11f1-80f3-ef30ccbee3a0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:50:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu condemns violence in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank</link><description>
It was a rare condemnation from what is widely seen as the most religious and ultranationalist government in Israel’s history. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu condemned recent attacks by Israeli settlers on Palestinians in the occupied West Bank, but described the violence as the actions of a “handful of rioters.” Tensions have surged across the territory, with activists accusing settlers of acting with impunity. Much of the recent violence has taken place in the town of Qusra. Peter O’Brien reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27abccec-a44f-11f1-958b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/israeli-settlers.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27abccec-a44f-11f1-958b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/israeli-settlers.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4c4f894-a44b-11f1-9470-75564c8cf08f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:46:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Niger: Junta says back in control after mutiny</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/niger-junta-says-back-in-control-after-mutiny</link><description>
Gunfire and explosions have been reported in Niger, as mutinying soldiers attempted to storm the presidential palace in the capital, Niamey, in a challenge to the ruling junta. The government said it had regained control after hours of fighting on Saturday. Léo Paichard and Nick Rushworth report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6de5a756-a44e-11f1-bda9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Niger-Junta.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6de5a756-a44e-11f1-bda9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Niger-Junta.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">91657b78-a44b-11f1-b67e-ef30ccbee3a0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:41:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Death toll rises as 3,000 remain missing in Nepal, China</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/death-toll-rises-as-3-000-remain-missing-in-nepal-china</link><description>
Rescue and relief efforts in Nepal and Tibet have been hampered this Sunday by heavy rain and rising river levels. The latest figures following Wednesday’s flash floods put the death toll at 750, while more than 3,000 people remain missing. Nepal’s disaster authorities are urging rescue teams to “exercise caution”, warning that bad weather, swollen rivers and the threat of further flooding could hamper operations. Shazab Wahlah reports from the town of Bidur.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca458a7e-a44a-11f1-927b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-090302-090512-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca458a7e-a44a-11f1-927b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-090302-090512-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf7d2614-a44a-11f1-bae8-ef30ccbee3a0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:37:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Manhunt underway after one killed, multiple injured at Swiss rave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-one-killed-five-injured-in-shooting-at-rave-in-switzerland</link><description>
At least one person was killed and five others injured, some seriously, in a shooting at a rave in the northern Swiss city of Aarau, police and local media reported Sunday. A major police operation is underway at the scene, with authorities urging residents to stay away from the area.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/368e6a4a-a43f-11f1-a6fc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242243077736.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/368e6a4a-a43f-11f1-a6fc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242243077736.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">00d1fa52-a43f-11f1-b5b8-d9aaf403daec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 06:52:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/368e6a4a-a43f-11f1-a6fc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242243077736.jpg">© Michael Buholzer/Keystone via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Putin, Xi set for Central Asia summit as Russia and China seek to counter Western influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260830-putin-xi-set-for-central-asia-summit-as-russia-china-seek-to-counter-western-influence</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping are due in Kyrgyzstan on Monday for a two-day summit, joined by the leaders of Iran and India. The gathering comes as the group seeks to project a united front amid wars in Ukraine and Iran and growing tensions with the West.
